From: SZL estate fix lane
Date: 2026-09-05
Subject: fix(frontend): extend the 44px hit-area floor to hero CTAs at mobile breakpoints

The mobile 44px hit-area floor (`.nav nav .btn{min-height:44px}`) only covers
nav CTAs. The hero CTA `Book an evidence pilot` (`a.btn.btn-ghost`) sits outside
`.nav`, so on the 360x800 viewport it renders at 43.17px and trips
code `PRIMARY_TARGET_UNDERSIZED` (issue #1359, canary 33988320849).

This adds one rule extending the same floor to hero action buttons at <=480px.
Desktop breakpoints are untouched. Apply with: git apply <this file>

Signed-off-by: SZL estate fix lane <noreply@szl-holdings>
---
diff --git a/a11oy_landing.html b/a11oy_landing.html
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/a11oy_landing.html
+++ b/a11oy_landing.html
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+  @media(max-width:480px){
+    .hero .btn, .actions .btn, .cta-row .btn{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:44px;min-width:44px}
+  }
